language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ knapsack: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A hiker is planning a trip and needs to decide which items to take in their backpack. Each item has a certain value and weight, and the hiker wants to maximise the total value of the items in the backpack without exceeding the weight capacity of the backpack.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `knapsack.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/knapsack.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `knapsack_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py knapsack.json
$   savilerow model.eprime knapsack_1.param -run-solver

$ weight capacity of the backpack
given capacity : int
$ values_dim1: the number of items (derived from the data); values[i]: value of item i, indices 1-based
given values_dim1 : int
given values : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of int
$ weights[i]: weight of item i, indices 1-based (the converter sizes it by values_dim1)
given weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of int

$ x[i]: item i is taken
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of bool
$ the total value of the items taken
find total : int(0..sum(values))

branching on [x]

maximising total
such that
$ the total weight of the items taken must not exceed the capacity of the backpack
(sum i : int(1..values_dim1) . toInt(x[i]) * weights[i]) <= capacity,
$ the total value is the sum of the values of the items taken
total = (sum i : int(1..values_dim1) . toInt(x[i]) * values[i])
